vidence":"ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\""},"featureId":"P0CU43.1:feature:10"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"159..177","start":159,"end":177,"segments":[{"start":159,"end":177}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"\"CAHS motif 2.","evidence":"ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\""},"featureId":"P0CU43.1:feature:11"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"200..224","start":200,"end":224,"segments":[{"start":200,"end":224}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite."},"featureId":"P0CU43.1:feature:12"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Compositionally biased region","locationText":"200..215","start":200,"end":215,"segments":[{"start":200,"end":215}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Compositionally biased region","note":"\"Low complexity.","evidence":"ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\""},"featureId":"P0CU43.1:feature:13"}],"sites":[],"otherFeatures":[],"featureSummary":{"total":13,"sources":1,"genes":1,"proteins":1,"regions":10,"sites":0,"otherFeatures":0}},"rawText":"LOCUS       CAHS3_HYPEX              224 aa            linear   INV 28-JAN-2026\nDEFINITION  RecName: Full=Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 77580;\n            Short=CAHS 77580; AltName: Full=Tardigrade-specific intrinsically\n            disordered protein CAHS 77580; Short=TDP CAHS 77580.\nACCESSION   P0CU43\nVERSION     P0CU43.1\nDBSOURCE    UniProtKB: locus CAHS3_HYPEX, accession P0CU43;\n            class: standard.\n            extra accessions:A0A1W0WTA5\n            created: Jun 7, 2017.\n            sequence updated: Jun 7, 2017.\n            annotation updated: Jan 28, 2026.\n            xrefs: MTYJ01000050.1, OQV18383.1\n            xrefs (non-sequence databases): AlphaFoldDB:P0CU43, SMR:P0CU43,\n            OrthoDB:10055812at2759, Proteomes:UP000192578, GO:0005737,\n            GO:0009269, DisProt:DP01378\nKEYWORDS    Coiled coil; Cytoplasm; Reference proteome; Repeat; Stress\n            response.\nSOURCE      Hypsibius exemplaris\n  ORGANISM  Hypsibius exemplaris\n            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Ecdysozoa; Tardigrada; Eutardigrada; Parachela;\n            Hypsibioidea; Hypsibiidae; Hypsibius.\nREFERENCE   1  (residues 1 to 224)\n  AUTHORS   Yoshida,Y., Koutsovoulos,G., Laetsch,D.R., Stevens,L., Kumar,S.,\n            Horikawa,D.D., Ishino,K., Komine,S., Kunieda,T., Tomita,M.,\n            Blaxter,M. and Arakawa,K.\n  TITLE     Comparative genomics of the tardigrades Hypsibius dujardini and\n            Ramazzottius varieornatus\n  JOURNAL   PLoS Biol 15 (7), e2002266 (2017)\n   PUBMED   28749982\n  REMARK    NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE [LARGE SCALE GENOMIC DNA].;\n            STRAIN=Z151\nREFERENCE   2  (residues 1 to 224)\n  AUTHORS   Boothby,T.C., Tapia,H., Brozena,A.H., Piszkiewicz,S., Smith,A.E.,\n            Giovannini,I., Rebecchi,L., Pielak,G.J., Koshland,D. and\n            Goldstein,B.\n  TITLE     Tardigrades Use Intrinsically Disordered Proteins to Survive\n            Desiccation\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 65 (6), 975-984 (2017)\n   PUBMED   28306513\n  REMARK    FUNCTION, INDUCTION, AND DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE.\nREFERENCE   3  (residues 1 to 224)\n  AUTHORS   Arakawa,K. and Numata,K.\n  TITLE     Reconsidering the 'glass transition' hypothesis of intrinsically\n            unstructured CAHS proteins in desiccation tolerance of tardigrades\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 81 (3), 409-410 (2021)\n   PUBMED   33545053\n  REMARK    FUNCTION.\nCOMMENT     [FUNCTION] CAHS proteins are cytosolic heat soluble proteins that\n            seem to contribute to the anhydrobiosis in tardigrades, but their\n            specific mechanisms are yet to be identified (PubMed:28306513,\n            PubMed:33545053). It is possible that protection during\n            anhydrobiosis might occur via the stabilization of vitrifying small\n            molecules such as sugars, but not via the direct glass transition\n            of CAHS proteins themselves (Probable).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053,\n            ECO:0000305|PubMed:33545053}.\n            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Cytoplasm {ECO:0000305|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [INDUCTION] Expression is highly induced during desiccation\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [DOMAIN] CAHS proteins contain 2 repeats of 19-mer peptides\n            designated as CAHS-motifs that comprise each two octapeptides\n            connected by a tripeptide (By similarity).\n            {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799}.\n            [DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE] Affects slightly survival under dry\n            conditions but does not affect survival under frozen conditions\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [MISCELLANEOUS] Trehalose, a disaccharide essential for several\n            organisms to survive drying, is detected at low levels or not at\n            all in some tardigrade species, indicating that tardigrades possess\n            potentially novel mechanisms for surviving desiccation involving\n            tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered proteins (TDPs)\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein\n            (CAHS) family. {ECO:0000305}.\n            [CAUTION] It was suggested that CAHS proteins were intrinsically\n            unstructured and show heat-dependent glass transition, which\n            contributes to the vitrification of cells, and this further leads\n            to desiccation tolerance (PubMed:28306513). However, more recent\n            studies led to the conclusion that there was no evidence supporting\n            glass transition of CAHS proteins to be contributing to the glass\n            transition of the whole tardigrade (PubMed:33545053).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053}.\nFEATURES             Location/Qualifiers\n     source          1..224\n                     /organism=\"Hypsibius exemplaris\"\n                     /db_xref=\"taxon:2072580\"\n     gene            1..224\n                     /gene=\"CAHS 77580\"\n                     /locus_tag=\"BV898_07587\"\n     Protein         1..224\n                     /product=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 77580\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS 77580; Tardigrade-specific intrinsically\n                     disordered protein CAHS 77580; TDP CAHS 77580\"\n                     /UniProtKB_evidence=\"Evidence at transcript level\"\n     Region          1..224\n                     /region_name=\"Mature chain\"\n                     /note=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 77580.\n                     /id=PRO_0000440192.\"\n     Region          1..38\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          1..13\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Low complexity.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          24..38\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Basic and acidic residues.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          <80..186\n                     /region_name=\"PTZ00491\"\n                     /note=\"major vault protein; Provisional\"\n                     /db_xref=\"CDD:240439\"\n     Region          83..191\n                     /region_name=\"Coiled-coil region\"\n                     /note=\"/evidence=ECO:0000255.\"\n     Region          122..140\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS motif 1.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\"\n     Region          159..177\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS motif 2.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\"\n     Region          200..224\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          200..215\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Low complexity.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\nORIGIN      \n        1 msnyqqessy qysdrsnngq qqeqqekkev ehssythtdv kvnmpnliap fisssaglaq\n       61 elvgegfqas vsritgasge ltvidteaet eearrdmeak areqellsrq fekelerkte\n      121 ayrkqqevet ekirkelekq hlrdvefrke lmeqtienqk rqidlearya kkelerernk\n      181 vkrvlerskf htdiqvnmea aagsthsgss svavsesekf qtnn\n//","fileName":"NCBI EFetch GenPept","recordIndex":10,"importedAt":"2026-11-02T16:29:24.734Z","sourceOrigin":{"type":"ncbi_efetch_genpept","name":"NCBI EFetch GenPept"}},"P0CU43":{"accession":"P0CU43","accessionVersion":"P0CU43.1","locus":"CAHS3_HYPEX 224 aa linear INV 28-JAN-2026","definition":"RecName: Full=Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 77580; Short=CAHS 77580; AltName: Full=Tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered protein CAHS 77580; Short=TDP CAHS 77580.","sourceName":"Hypsibius exemplaris","organism":"Hypsibius exemplaris","lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Ecdysozoa","Tardigrada","Eutardigrada","Parachela","Hypsibioidea","Hypsibiidae","Hypsibius"],"taxid":"2072580","sequenceLength":224,"sequence":"MSNYQQESS