],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite."},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:6"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Compositionally biased region","locationText":"111..125","start":111,"end":125,"segments":[{"start":111,"end":125}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Compositionally biased region","note":"\"Basic and acidic residues.","evidence":"ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\""},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:7"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Coiled-coil region","locationText":"115..193","start":115,"end":193,"segments":[{"start":115,"end":193}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Coiled-coil region","note":"/evidence=ECO:0000255."},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:8"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"124..142","start":124,"end":142,"segments":[{"start":124,"end":142}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"\"CAHS motif 1.","evidence":"ECO:0000305|PubMed:22937162.\""},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:9"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"161..179","start":161,"end":179,"segments":[{"start":161,"end":179}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"\"CAHS motif 2.","evidence":"ECO:0000305|PubMed:22937162.\""},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:10"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"204..237","start":204,"end":237,"segments":[{"start":204,"end":237}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite."},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:11"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Compositionally biased region","locationText":"204..215","start":204,"end":215,"segments":[{"start":204,"end":215}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Compositionally biased region","note":"\"Low complexity.","evidence":"ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\""},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:12"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Compositionally biased region","locationText":"216..237","start":216,"end":237,"segments":[{"start":216,"end":237}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Compositionally biased region","note":"\"Basic and acidic residues.","evidence":"ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\""},"featureId":"P0CU46.2:feature:13"}],"sites":[],"otherFeatures":[],"featureSummary":{"total":13,"sources":1,"genes":1,"proteins":1,"regions":10,"sites":0,"otherFeatures":0}},"rawText":"LOCUS       CAHS2_HYPEX              237 aa            linear   INV 02-SEP-2026\nDEFINITION  RecName: Full=Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 86272;\n            Short=CAHS 86272; AltName: Full=Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble\n            protein b; Short=SAHS-b; AltName: Full=Tardigrade-specific\n            intrinsically disordered protein CAHS 86272; Short=TDP CAHS 86272.\nACCESSION   P0CU46\nVERSION     P0CU46.2\nDBSOURCE    UniProtKB: locus CAHS2_HYPEX, accession P0CU46;\n            class: standard.\n            extra accessions:A0A1W0X742\n            created: Jun 7, 2017.\n            sequence updated: Jan 28, 2026.\n            annotation updated: Sep 2, 2026.\n            xrefs: MTYJ01000013.1, OQV23218.1\n            xrefs (non-sequence databases): AlphaFoldDB:P0CU46,\n            OrthoDB:10456443at2759, Proteomes:UP000192578, GO:0005737,\n            GO:0009269, DisProt:DP01381\nKEYWORDS    Coiled coil; Cytoplasm; Reference proteome; Repeat; Stress\n            response.\nSOURCE      Hypsibius exemplaris\n  ORGANISM  Hypsibius exemplaris\n            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Ecdysozoa; Tardigrada; Eutardigrada; Parachela;\n            Hypsibioidea; Hypsibiidae; Hypsibius.\nREFERENCE   1  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Yoshida,Y., Koutsovoulos,G., Laetsch,D.R., Stevens,L., Kumar,S.,\n            Horikawa,D.D., Ishino,K., Komine,S., Kunieda,T., Tomita,M.,\n            Blaxter,M. and Arakawa,K.\n  TITLE     Comparative genomics of the tardigrades Hypsibius dujardini and\n            Ramazzottius varieornatus\n  JOURNAL   PLoS Biol 15 (7), e2002266 (2017)\n   PUBMED   28749982\n  REMARK    NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE [LARGE SCALE GENOMIC DNA].;\n            STRAIN=Z151\nREFERENCE   2  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Yamaguchi,A., Tanaka,S., Yamaguchi,S., Kuwahara,H., Takamura,C.,\n            Imajoh-Ohmi,S., Horikawa,D.D., Toyoda,A., Katayama,T., Arakawa,K.,\n            Fujiyama,A., Kubo,T. and Kunieda,T.\n  TITLE     Two novel heat-soluble protein families abundantly expressed in an\n            anhydrobiotic tardigrade\n  JOURNAL   PLoS One 7 (8), e44209 (2012)\n   PUBMED   22937162\n  REMARK    DOMAIN.\nREFERENCE   3  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Boothby,T.C., Tapia,H., Brozena,A.H., Piszkiewicz,S., Smith,A.E.,\n            Giovannini,I., Rebecchi,L., Pielak,G.J., Koshland,D. and\n            Goldstein,B.\n  TITLE     Tardigrades Use Intrinsically Disordered Proteins to Survive\n            Desiccation\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 65 (6), 975-984 (2017)\n   PUBMED   28306513\n  REMARK    FUNCTION, INDUCTION, AND DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE.\nREFERENCE   4  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Arakawa,K. and Numata,K.\n  TITLE     Reconsidering the 'glass transition' hypothesis of intrinsically\n            unstructured CAHS proteins in desiccation tolerance of tardigrades\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 81 (3), 409-410 (2021)\n   PUBMED   33545053\n  REMARK    FUNCTION.\nCOMMENT     On Jan 30, 2026 this sequence version replaced P0CU46.1.\n            [FUNCTION] CAHS proteins are cytosolic heat soluble proteins that\n            seem to contribute to the anhydrobiosis in tardigrades, but their\n            specific mechanisms are yet to be identified (PubMed:28306513,\n            PubMed:33545053). It is possible that protection during\n            anhydrobiosis might occur via the stabilization of vitrifying small\n            molecules such as sugars, but not via the direct glass transition\n            of CAHS proteins themselves (Probable).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053,\n            ECO:0000305|PubMed:33545053}.\n            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Cytoplasm {ECO:0000305|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [INDUCTION] Expression is highly induced during desiccation\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [DOMAIN] CAHS proteins contain 2 repeats of 19-mer peptides\n            designated as CAHS-motifs that comprise each two octapeptides\n            connected by a tripeptide (PubMed:22937162).\n            {ECO:0000305|PubMed:22937162}.\n            [DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE] Affects slightly survival under dry\n            conditions but does not affect survival under frozen conditions\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [MISCELLANEOUS] Trehalose, a disaccharide essential for several\n            organisms to survive drying, is detected at low levels or not at\n            all in some tardigrade species, indicating that tardigrades possess\n            potentially novel mechanisms for surviving desiccation involving\n            tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered proteins (TDPs)\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein\n            (CAHS) family. {ECO:0000305}.\n            [CAUTION] It was suggested that CAHS proteins were intrinsically\n            unstructured and show heat-dependent glass transition, which\n            contributes to the vitrification of cells, and this further leads\n            to desiccation tolerance (PubMed:28306513). However, more recent\n            studies led to the conclusion that there was no evidence supporting\n            glass transition of CAHS proteins to be contributing to the glass\n            transition of the whole tardigrade (PubMed:33545053).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053}.\nFEATURES             Location/Qualifiers\n     source          1..237\n                     /organism=\"Hypsibius exemplaris\"\n                     /db_xref=\"taxon:2072580\"\n     gene            1..237\n                     /gene=\"CAHS 86272\"\n                     /locus_tag=\"BV898_02951\"\n                     /gene_synonym=\"CAHS-b\"\n     Protein         1..237\n                     /product=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 86272\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS 86272; Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein\n                     b; Tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered protein\n                     CAHS 86272; SAHS-b; TDP CAHS 86272\"\n                     /UniProtKB_evidence=\"Evidence at transcript level\"\n     Region          1..237\n                     /region_name=\"Mature chain\"\n                     /note=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 86272.\n                     /id=PRO_0000440191.\"\n     Region          <82..191\n                     /region_name=\"PTZ00491\"\n                     /note=\"major vault protein; Provisional\"\n                     /db_xref=\"CDD:240439\"\n     Region          96..125\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n        