ocationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"ATP-synt_Fo_b","note":"F-type ATP synthase, membrane subunit b; cl21478","db_xref":"CDD:473877"},"featureId":"J7M799.1:feature:10"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"132..150","start":132,"end":150,"segments":[{"start":132,"end":150}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"\"CAHS motif 1.","evidence":"ECO:0000305|PubMed:22937162.\""},"featureId":"J7M799.1:feature:11"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"169..187","start":169,"end":187,"segments":[{"start":169,"end":187}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"\"CAHS motif 2.","evidence":"ECO:0000305|PubMed:22937162.\""},"featureId":"J7M799.1:feature:12"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"212..237","start":212,"end":237,"segments":[{"start":212,"end":237}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite."},"featureId":"J7M799.1:feature:13"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Compositionally biased region","locationText":"226..237","start":226,"end":237,"segments":[{"start":226,"end":237}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Compositionally biased region","note":"\"Basic and acidic residues.","evidence":"ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\""},"featureId":"J7M799.1:feature:14"}],"sites":[],"otherFeatures":[],"featureSummary":{"total":14,"sources":1,"genes":1,"proteins":1,"regions":11,"sites":0,"otherFeatures":0}},"rawText":"LOCUS       CAHS1_RAMVA              237 aa            linear   INV 02-SEP-2026\nDEFINITION  RecName: Full=Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 1;\n            Short=CAHS1; AltName: Full=Tardigrade-specific intrinsically\n            disordered protein CAHS1; Short=TDP CAHS1.\nACCESSION   J7M799\nVERSION     J7M799.1\nDBSOURCE    UniProtKB: locus CAHS1_RAMVA, accession J7M799;\n            class: standard.\n            created: Jun 7, 2017.\n            sequence updated: Oct 31, 2012.\n            annotation updated: Sep 2, 2026.\n            xrefs: AB650499.1, BAM37958.1, BDGG01000001.1, GAU88202.1\n            xrefs (non-sequence databases): AlphaFoldDB:J7M799, SMR:J7M799,\n            Proteomes:UP000186922, GO:0005737, GO:0005634, DisProt:DP01377\nKEYWORDS    Coiled coil; Cytoplasm; Nucleus; Reference proteome; Repeat; Stress\n            response.\nSOURCE      Ramazzottius varieornatus\n  ORGANISM  Ramazzottius varieornatus\n            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Ecdysozoa; Tardigrada; Eutardigrada; Parachela;\n            Hypsibioidea; Ramazzottiidae; Ramazzottius.\nREFERENCE   1  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Yamaguchi,A., Tanaka,S., Yamaguchi,S., Kuwahara,H., Takamura,C.,\n            Imajoh-Ohmi,S., Horikawa,D.D., Toyoda,A., Katayama,T., Arakawa,K.,\n            Fujiyama,A., Kubo,T. and Kunieda,T.\n  TITLE     Two novel heat-soluble protein families abundantly expressed in an\n            anhydrobiotic tardigrade\n  JOURNAL   PLoS One 7 (8), e44209 (2012)\n   PUBMED   22937162\n  REMARK    NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE [MRNA], IDENTIFICATION BY MASS SPECTROMETRY,\n            FUNCTION, DOMAIN, AND SUBCELLULAR LOCATION.;\n            STRAIN=YOKOZUNA-1\nREFERENCE   2  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Hashimoto,T., Horikawa,D.D., Saito,Y., Kuwahara,H., Kozuka-Hata,H.,\n            Shin-I,T., Minakuchi,Y., Ohishi,K., Motoyama,A., Aizu,T.,\n            Enomoto,A., Kondo,K., Tanaka,S., Hara,Y., Koshikawa,S., Sagara,H.,\n            Miura,T., Yokobori,S.I., Miyagawa,K., Suzuki,Y., Kubo,T., Oyama,M.,\n            Kohara,Y., Fujiyama,A., Arakawa,K., Katayama,T., Toyoda,A. and\n            Kunieda,T.\n  TITLE     Extremotolerant tardigrade genome and improved radiotolerance of\n            human cultured cells by tardigrade-unique protein\n  JOURNAL   Nat Commun 7, 12808 (2016)\n   PUBMED   27649274\n  REMARK    NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE [LARGE SCALE GENOMIC DNA].;\n            STRAIN=YOKOZUNA-1\nREFERENCE   3  (residues 1 to 237)\n  AUTHORS   Arakawa,K. and Numata,K.\n  TITLE     Reconsidering the 'glass transition' hypothesis of intrinsically\n            unstructured CAHS proteins in desiccation tolerance of tardigrades\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 81 (3), 409-410 (2021)\n   PUBMED   33545053\n  REMARK    FUNCTION.\nCOMMENT     [FUNCTION] CAHS proteins are cytosolic heat soluble proteins that\n            seem to contribute to the anhydrobiosis in tardigrades, but their\n            specific mechanisms are yet to be identified (PubMed:22937162,\n            PubMed:33545053). It is possible that protection during\n            anhydrobiosis might occur via the stabilization of vitrifying small\n            molecules such as sugars, but not via the direct glass transition\n            of CAHS proteins themselves (Probable).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:22937162, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053,\n            ECO:0000305|PubMed:33545053}.\n            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Cytoplasm {ECO:0000269|PubMed:22937162}.\n            Nucleus {ECO:0000269|PubMed:22937162}. Note=Is distributed mostly\n            in the cytoplasm and weakly in the nucleus (PubMed:22937162).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:22937162}.\n            [DOMAIN] CAHS proteins contain 2 repeats of 19-mer peptides\n            designated as CAHS-motifs that comprise each two octapeptides\n            connected by a tripeptide (PubMed:22937162).\n            {ECO:0000305|PubMed:22937162}.\n            [MISCELLANEOUS] Trehalose, a disaccharide essential for several\n            organisms to survive drying, is detected at low levels or not at\n            all in some tardigrade species, indicating that tardigrades possess\n            potentially novel mechanisms for surviving desiccation involving\n            tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered proteins (TDPs) (By\n            similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P0CU44}.\n            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein\n            (CAHS) family. {ECO:0000305}.\nFEATURES             Location/Qualifiers\n     source          1..237\n                     /organism=\"Ramazzottius varieornatus\"\n                     /db_xref=\"taxon:947166\"\n     gene            1..237\n                     /gene=\"CAHS1\"\n                     /locus_tag=\"RvY_00944\"\n     Protein         1..237\n                     /product=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 1\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS1; Tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered\n                     protein CAHS1; TDP CAHS1\"\n                     /UniProtKB_evidence=\"Evidence at protein level\"\n     Region          1..237\n                     /region_name=\"Mature chain\"\n                     /note=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 1.\n                     /id=PRO_0000440187.\"\n     Region          1..35\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          1..17\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Basic and acidic residues.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          85..105\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          91..105\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n               