0","start":342,"end":360,"segments":[{"start":342,"end":360}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"\"CAHS motif 2.","evidence":"ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\""},"featureId":"P0CU47.2:feature:13"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Region of interest in the sequence","locationText":"388..414","start":388,"end":414,"segments":[{"start":388,"end":414}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Region of interest in the sequence","note":"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite."},"featureId":"P0CU47.2:feature:14"},{"featureType":"Region","featureClass":"region","label":"Compositionally biased region","locationText":"388..405","start":388,"end":405,"segments":[{"start":388,"end":405}],"locationOperator":"simple","locationStatus":"supported","locationVersion":1,"qualifiers":{"region_name":"Compositionally biased region","note":"\"Polar residues.","evidence":"ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\""},"featureId":"P0CU47.2:feature:15"}],"sites":[],"otherFeatures":[],"featureSummary":{"total":15,"sources":1,"genes":1,"proteins":1,"regions":12,"sites":0,"otherFeatures":0}},"rawText":"LOCUS       CAHS5_HYPEX              414 aa            linear   INV 02-SEP-2026\nDEFINITION  RecName: Full=Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 89226;\n            Short=CAHS 89226; AltName: Full=Tardigrade-specific intrinsically\n            disordered protein CAHS 89226; Short=TDP CAHS 89226.\nACCESSION   P0CU47\nVERSION     P0CU47.2\nDBSOURCE    UniProtKB: locus CAHS5_HYPEX, accession P0CU47;\n            class: standard.\n            extra accessions:A0A1W0WNR6,A0A1W0WNT0\n            created: Jun 7, 2017.\n            sequence updated: Jan 28, 2026.\n            annotation updated: Sep 2, 2026.\n            xrefs: MTYJ01000069.1, OQV16865.1, OQV16866.1\n            xrefs (non-sequence databases): AlphaFoldDB:P0CU47,\n            OrthoDB:10590680at2759, Proteomes:UP000192578, GO:0005737,\n            DisProt:DP01382\nKEYWORDS    Coiled coil; Cytoplasm; Reference proteome; Repeat; Stress\n            response.\nSOURCE      Hypsibius exemplaris\n  ORGANISM  Hypsibius exemplaris\n            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Ecdysozoa; Tardigrada; Eutardigrada; Parachela;\n            Hypsibioidea; Hypsibiidae; Hypsibius.\nREFERENCE   1  (residues 1 to 414)\n  AUTHORS   Yoshida,Y., Koutsovoulos,G., Laetsch,D.R., Stevens,L., Kumar,S.,\n            Horikawa,D.D., Ishino,K., Komine,S., Kunieda,T., Tomita,M.,\n            Blaxter,M. and Arakawa,K.\n  TITLE     Comparative genomics of the tardigrades Hypsibius dujardini and\n            Ramazzottius varieornatus\n  JOURNAL   PLoS Biol 15 (7), e2002266 (2017)\n   PUBMED   28749982\n  REMARK    NUCLEOTIDE SEQUENCE [LARGE SCALE GENOMIC DNA].;\n            STRAIN=Z151\nREFERENCE   2  (residues 1 to 414)\n  AUTHORS   Boothby,T.C., Tapia,H., Brozena,A.H., Piszkiewicz,S., Smith,A.E.,\n            Giovannini,I., Rebecchi,L., Pielak,G.J., Koshland,D. and\n            Goldstein,B.\n  TITLE     Tardigrades Use Intrinsically Disordered Proteins to Survive\n            Desiccation\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 65 (6), 975-984 (2017)\n   PUBMED   28306513\n  REMARK    FUNCTION.\nREFERENCE   3  (residues 1 to 414)\n  AUTHORS   Arakawa,K. and Numata,K.\n  TITLE     Reconsidering the 'glass transition' hypothesis of intrinsically\n            unstructured CAHS proteins in desiccation tolerance of tardigrades\n  JOURNAL   Mol Cell 81 (3), 409-410 (2021)\n   PUBMED   33545053\n  REMARK    FUNCTION.\nCOMMENT     On Jan 30, 2026 this sequence version replaced P0CU47.1.\n            [FUNCTION] CAHS proteins are cytosolic heat soluble proteins that\n            seem to contribute to the anhydrobiosis in tardigrades, but their\n            specific mechanisms are yet to be identified (PubMed:28306513,\n            PubMed:33545053). It is possible that protection during\n            anhydrobiosis might occur via the stabilization of vitrifying small\n            molecules such as sugars, but not via the direct glass transition\n            of CAHS proteins themselves (Probable).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053,\n            ECO:0000305|PubMed:33545053}.\n            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Cytoplasm {ECO:0000305|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [DOMAIN] CAHS proteins contain 2 repeats of 19-mer peptides\n            designated as CAHS-motifs that comprise each two octapeptides\n            connected by a tripeptide (By similarity).\n            {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799}.\n            [MISCELLANEOUS] Trehalose, a disaccharide essential for several\n            organisms to survive drying, is detected at low levels or not at\n            all in some tardigrade species, indicating that tardigrades possess\n            potentially novel mechanisms for surviving desiccation involving\n            tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered proteins (TDPs)\n            (PubMed:28306513). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513}.\n            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein\n            (CAHS) family. {ECO:0000305}.\n            [CAUTION] It was suggested that CAHS proteins were intrinsically\n            unstructured and show heat-dependent glass transition, which\n            contributes to the vitrification of cells, and this further leads\n            to desiccation tolerance (PubMed:28306513). However, more recent\n            studies led to the conclusion that there was no evidence supporting\n            glass transition of CAHS proteins to be contributing to the glass\n            transition of the whole tardigrade (PubMed:33545053).\n            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:28306513, ECO:0000269|PubMed:33545053}.\n            [SEQUENCE CAUTION] Sequence=OQV16865.1; Type=Erroneous gene model\n            prediction; Note=The predicted genes BV898_09037 and BV898_09038\n            have been merged into 1 gene: CAHS 89226.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};\n            Sequence=OQV16866.1; Type=Erroneous gene model prediction; Note=The\n            predicted genes BV898_09037 and BV898_09038 have been merged into 1\n            gene: CAHS 89226.; Evidence={ECO:0000305}.\nFEATURES             Location/Qualifiers\n     source          1..414\n                     /organism=\"Hypsibius exemplaris\"\n                     /db_xref=\"taxon:2072580\"\n     gene            1..414\n                     /gene=\"CAHS 89226\"\n                     /locus_tag=\"BV898_09037/BV898_09038\"\n     Protein         1..414\n                     /product=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 89226\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS 89226; Tardigrade-specific intrinsically\n                     disordered protein CAHS 89226; TDP CAHS 89226\"\n                     /UniProtKB_evidence=\"Inferred from homology\"\n     Region          1..414\n                     /region_name=\"Mature chain\"\n                     /note=\"Cytosolic-abundant heat soluble protein 89226.\n                     /id=PRO_0000440194.\"\n     Region          25..155\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          27..45\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Basic and acidic residues.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          69..84\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Basic and acidic residues.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          86..101\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Low complexity.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          120..134\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Low complexity.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          142..155\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Polar residues.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          305..323\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS motif 1.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\"\n     Region          341..376\n                     /region_name=\"Coiled-coil region\"\n                     /note=\"/evidence=ECO:0000255.\"\n     Region          342..360\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"CAHS motif 2.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:J7M799.\"\n     Region          388..414\n                     /region_name=\"Region of interest in the sequence\"\n                     /note=\"Disordered. /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\n     Region          388..405\n                     /region_name=\"Compositionally biased region\"\n                     /note=\"Polar residues.\n                     /evidence=ECO:0000256|SAM:MobiDB-lite.\"\nORIGIN      \n        1 matkeskyer vekvnvdadg atlvkniged rgkedpgmny qdkrpanlvp gapagvipnr\n       61 ieslptdrag qrlrehlses erlrgsrsst ssksssfvep slkyrgeigp igkngefvas\n      121 snrqnsssnv sssdnseras pasrnsnpgm nngmttqrtt vitessvqgl gaqrtvpiqp\n      181 hqqredhevi thesharape ttvvtipttr fesaqlesrr dgrtytedke ltipapvvap\n      241 qihahqqvnm sggtsatiha ttdlhlasea qindmgpeey eryrakveal arihedetsr\n      301 kaaayrnave adaelirqtl erqhmrdief rkdlvessvd rqqqeirlea eyamraleqe\n      361 rvnaraaldq amastnidvn idsaigtths qgrvtttses rtsqargpat aavi\n//","fileName":"NCBI EFetch GenPept","recordIndex":84,"importedAt":"2026-11-02T16:29:24.737Z