\n  ORGANISM  Lampetra fluviatilis\n            Eukaryota; Metazoa; Chordata; Craniata; Vertebrata; Cyclostomata;\n            Hyperoartia; Petromyzontiformes; Petromyzontidae; Lampetra.\nREFERENCE   1\n  CONSRTM   ELIXIR-Norway, Elixir Norway\n  TITLE     Direct Submission\n  JOURNAL   Submitted (13-MAR-2025) ELIXIR-Norway, Thormoehlens gt 55, 5008\n            Bergen, Norway\nCOMMENT     This project provides the diploid genome assembly kcLamFluv2.2 of\n            the river lamprey, Lampetra fluviatilis. The sample was provided by\n            Eivind Schartum, and the data generation and assembly were carried\n            out by EBP-Nor (https://www.ebpnor.org/). kcLamFluv2.2 is based on\n            38x PacBio HiFi data and 100x Arima Hi-C data. The HiFi reads were\n            filtered for adapters using HiFiAdapterFilt, and assembled with\n            hifiasm along with Hi-C data to generate a pair of\n            haplotype-resolved assemblies. K-mers from the two assemblies were\n            used to filter Hi-C reads to create two sets of reads for\n            scaffolding the assemblies (i.e., reads used to scaffold hap1 did\n            not contain k-mers unique to hap2). YaHS was used for scaffolding.\n            FCS-adaptor was used to remove putative adapters, and putative\n            contaminants were removed with FCS-GX. The chromosomes confirmed by\n            Hi-C data are named according to size.\nFEATURES             Location/Qualifiers\n     source          1..1401\n                     /organism=\"Lampetra fluviatilis\"\n                     /db_xref=\"taxon:7748\"\n                     /chromosome=\"63\"\n                     /geo_loc_name=\"Norway:Telemark, Asdalsaa\"\n                     /collection_date=\"2021-04-21\"\n     Protein         1..1401\n                     /name=\"unnamed protein product\"\n     Region          14..48\n                     /region_name=\"SAP\"\n                     /note=\"Putative DNA-binding (bihelical) mot